# Nextora — theme.json and HTML templates

- **Hybrid theme:** Classic PHP shells (`header.php`, `footer.php`, etc.) load block **template parts** from `parts/*.html` where applicable — align Site Editor structure with those parts.
- **Design tokens:** Colors, typography, spacing, and `layout.contentSize` / `wideSize` live in [`theme.json`](../../theme.json). Mirror important colors/fonts in `resources/css/app.css` `@theme` so Tailwind utilities match the editor.
- **Patterns:** Prefer core blocks and existing theme blocks; keep constrained layout compatibility (avoid fighting `layout` / content width unnecessarily).

```text
❌ Hard-code a hex in parts/header.html for theme-wide ink
✅ Use theme palette / classes that resolve via presets and @theme
```
